! pythia8_sm_fcc.cmnd
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Pythia8 steering for Stage-2 FCC-ee SM inclusive background.
! Reads the multi-process parton-level LHE from Stage 1 (MadGraph), applies
! the parton shower, decays all unstable particles, hadronizes final states,
! and writes HepMC2 for Delphes.
!
! Decay handling (all via Pythia8 internal tables, SM branching ratios):
!   W+/-  -> l nu (all flavours), q q' (all CKM-allowed)
!   Z     -> l+l-, nu nu~, q q~ (all flavours)
!   H(125)-> bb~ (58%), WW* (21%), gg (8%), ta+ta- (6%), cc~ (3%), ZZ* (3%), ...
!   tau   -> pi nu, mu nu nu, e nu nu, multi-hadron modes
! W, Z, H enter the LHE as undecayed status-2 intermediates; Pythia reads their
! PDG codes and decays them before showering the decay products.
!
! ISR/FSR: on (Pythia defaults). At sqrt(s)=240 GeV, ISR shifts the effective
! CM energy by O(alpha/pi) per emission; FSR produces soft QED radiation off
! charged final-state particles. Both are physical and are kept.
! MPI: off per project convention (e+e- has no underlying event).
! Hadronization: on (default; explicit here for clarity).
!
! Run through the driver:  bash mc/shower_background_sm_fcc.sh
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

! --- Input: multi-process LHE from Stage 1 ---
Beams:frameType = 4
Beams:LHEF      = PROC_background_sm_fcc/Events/run_01/unweighted_events.lhe.gz

! --- Statistics ---
Main:numberOfEvents   = 5000
Main:numberOfSubruns  = 1
Main:subrun           = 0
Main:timesAllowErrors = 10

! --- Shower, decays, hadronization ---
! HadronLevel:Hadronize is the Pythia8 default (on); stated explicitly so the
! difference from the mumu/ALP cards (where hadronization is irrelevant) is clear.
HadronLevel:Hadronize = on
PartonLevel:MPI       = off

! --- Robustness ---
Check:epTolErr = 2e-2
